 "answer": "In 2023, the FDA received **77 death reports** for pacemakers (LWP). That is 0.6% of the 12,633 LWP reports received that year.\n\nHow the 2023 LWP reports break down by event type:\n- Injury: 7,630 (60.4%)\n- Malfunction: 4,925 (39.0%)\n- Death: 77 (0.6%)\n- Other: 1 (0.0%)\n\nKeep in mind:\n- A death report means a pacemaker may have been involved. It doesn't prove the device caused the death. Many of these patients have serious underlying heart disease.\n- Report counts aren't failure rates, because there's no count of how many devices are in use.\n- These numbers are based on the date the FDA received each report, not the date of the event.\n\nI can also break these death reports down by manufacturer or failure mode, or pull example narratives.",
